  "insight": "The national total fertility rate fell from 1.205 in 2014 to 0.721 in 2023. The steepest large-cohort declines are in ages 25-29 and 30-34, while ages 40-44 rose from 5.2 to 7.9 births per 1,000 women, indicating both lower overall fertility and later childbearing."
